# The browser only ever receives the opaque atlas_session cookie from the API.
# It never sees a principal, a token, a capability handle, or a unit of work, so
# there is no VITE_ variable that should ever carry authority. This file names
# only the *server* configuration the dev login route reads, for the operator's
# benefit, and none of it belongs in the frontend bundle.
#
# Server side (src/atlas_web), NOT this app:
#   ATLAS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://atlas:atlas@127.0.0.1:5433/atlas_hq
#   ATLAS_WEB_DEV_LOGIN=1
#   ATLAS_WEB_OPERATOR_PRINCIPAL=atlas.local.operator
#
# This app (optional, affects nothing security-bearing):
#   ATLAS_WEB_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000   # Vite dev-server proxy target
